{{/*
  silent-notify-only — the two-bullet preamble that appears in the SILENT
  branch of ~20 Interaction Mode blocks: use only `mitto_ui_notify`, do NOT
  use interactive/blocking UI tools.

  Callers include this INSIDE their silent branch, then append any
  prompt-specific extras (autonomy criteria, stop-iterating hooks, etc.).

    {{- if and .Session.IsLoop (not .Session.IsLoopForced) }}
    **Silent mode** — a scheduled loop run; the user is not watching.
    {{ template "_shared/silent-notify-only" . }}
    - <prompt-specific extras here>
    {{- else }}
    ...
    {{- end }}

  This fragment intentionally emits only the two universal bullets so callers
  can attach as much (or as little) prompt-specific guidance as they need.
*/}}
- Use **only** `mitto_ui_notify` — non-blocking notifications only.
- Do **NOT** use `mitto_ui_options`, `mitto_ui_form`, `mitto_ui_textbox`, or
  any interactive/blocking UI tool. They will stall an unattended run.
